-- title:
--   Injectivity of W₀llbracket trrbracket → C for a representing algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $W_0$. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with the ideal $\bot$ installed as ambient ideal there is a unit power series $u$ with $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q = u \cdot F_0.\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\,q\,0\,0$, and let $F^u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$. Let $C$ be a local $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$-algebra, finite as a module over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ and complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, equipped with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_C : C \to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal of $C$ and satisfying $\mathrm{res}_C(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,f) = \mathrm{res}_0(\mathrm{constantCoeff}\,f)$ for all $f$; let $G_c$ over $C$ be the coefficientwise image of $F^u$ along the structure map, and let $c_0, c_1$ lie in the maximal ideal of $C$ with $G_c.\mathrm{IsDrinfeldBasisAdic}$ for the maximal ideal of $C$, $q$, $c_0$, $c_1$. Assume further the universal property: for every local $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$-algebra $B$ complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, every formal group law $G$ over $B$ that is the coefficientwise image of $F^u$, and all $y_0, y_1$ in the maximal ideal of $B$ with $G.\mathrm{IsDrinfeldBasisAdic}$ for the maximal ideal of $B$, $q$, $y_0$, $y_1$, there is a unique $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : C \to B$ with $\chi(c_0) = y_0$ and $\chi(c_1) = y_1$. Then the structure map $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket \to C$ is injective.
--
--   The algebra $C$ plays the role of the finite local algebra representing formal Drinfeld bases of level $q$ for the universal deformation $F^u$ over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$; the statement records that such a representing algebra is faithful over the base, so that relations in $C$ can be tested against $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$. It feeds the study of algebra homomorphisms out of $C$ over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$.
